{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-7fa09626193b261b0549","statement":"Let $m, r \\geq 2$, $k,s,p,q,h \\in \\Gamma_\\mu \\subset \\C$. Then\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{i=0}^m \\sum_{j=0}^r (-1)^{i+j} {m \\choose i} {r \\choose j}\n\\left( \\left\\{ \\Omega^{(m,h)}_{k-ih,s-jh} , \\Omega^{(r,h)}_{q+ih,p+jh} \\right\\}\n-       \\left\\{ \\Omega^{(m,h)}_{k-ih,q-jh} , \\Omega^{(r,h)}_{s+ih,p+jh} \\right\\} \\right)  \\\\\n= (q-s) \\left( (p-k+2rh) \\Omega^{(2m+2r-1,h)}_{k+p+2rh,s+q-2rh}\n-  (p-k+2mh) \\Omega^{(2m+2r-1,h)}_{k+p+(2r-1)h,s+q-(2r-1)h} \\right) .\n\\end{align*}","source_id":"arXiv:1304.5458","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"d0932de228f7922207aa181f43cb3af0a4fd226aa22c4490297cbf57479e0e04","kind":"theorem","label":"Theorem 13","ref_key":"solfor","name":"","order":17,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.5458","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"865c1339c4d68e405e38c5eee308a728d2ef4a51ce89ebdecfba4934c3dac634","line":557,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:11:24+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":463,"math_hints":50}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1304.5458","title":"Classification of simple $W_n$-modules with finite-dimensional weight spaces","abstract":"We classify all simple $W_n$-modules with finite-dimensional weight spaces. Every such module is either of a highest weight type or is a quotient of a module of tensor fields on a torus, which was conjectured by Eswara Rao. This generalizes the classical result of Mathieu on simple weight modules for the Virasoro algebra. In our proof of the classification we construct a functor from the category of cuspidal $W_n$-modules to the category of $W_n$-modules with a compatible action of the algebra of functions on a torus. We also present a new identity for certain quadratic elements in t